WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Translator: Denise RQ
Reviewer: Csaba Lóki

00:00:10.356 --> 00:00:13.016
"When the cheetah
got a glimpse of the gazelles,

00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:15.336
it stirred its hunting instinct,

00:00:15.336 --> 00:00:18.326
and it slid off the rock 
covered by bush so silently

00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:21.011
that we didn't hear the slightest sound.

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:23.871
Stretching its slim body 
as far out as possible,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.560
lying low, it sneaked quickly, 
without any noise towards the gazelles.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.070
Its eyes locked on them, 
and it used every hollow, small bush,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.200
and larger tussock to remain concealed.

00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:41.831
And it succeeded; the gazelles
continued to graze on calmly.

00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:45.881
It crawled forward like a shadow,

00:00:45.881 --> 00:00:51.561
and even with the ruffle of the grass,
nothing was suspected.

00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:57.841
When it was 30 - 40 steps away from them,
it lunged forward like an uncoiled spring.

00:00:57.851 --> 00:00:59.951
Into the herd with some quick jumps,

00:00:59.951 --> 00:01:03.014
and grabbed one of the females 
that it had spotted earlier.

00:01:03.274 --> 00:01:06.884
But the gazelle escaped,
and the whole herd started a mad dash.

00:01:07.444 --> 00:01:10.684
The cheetah ran next to the gazelle
with beautiful strides,

00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:13.954
and after a 200-step pace, 
it grabbed the gazelle by the throat,

00:01:13.964 --> 00:01:16.514
and knocked her down with its paw."

00:01:18.254 --> 00:01:21.924
I think this was the moment 
when I fell in love with Africa forever.

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:25.354
Because my father didn't read 
traditional bedtime stories to me.

00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:28.464
Instead, the stories of hunter authors
such as Zsigmond Széchenyi,

00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:31.934
Jim Corbett, or Ferenc Donászy
whom I've just mentioned.

00:01:32.244 --> 00:01:34.584
Thanks to these stories, all of my life, 

00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:37.354
I have been dreaming
about someday getting to Africa

00:01:37.354 --> 00:01:43.741
to see the endless savannas, the wildlife,
and the snow-covered peak of Kilimanjaro.

00:01:44.911 --> 00:01:48.601
Time passed by,
and this remained a dream.

00:01:49.721 --> 00:01:51.871
Years later, I was working
for a TV station,

00:01:51.871 --> 00:01:54.021
where I did a series of interviews

00:01:54.021 --> 00:01:57.441
in which I talked with people 
who are interesting and important to me.

00:01:57.441 --> 00:02:01.251
This is how one evening, I hosted 
our legendary alpinist, Zsolt Erőss.

00:02:01.511 --> 00:02:04.781
After the interview, we were talking 
in the corridor and I told him,

00:02:04.781 --> 00:02:07.951
"You know, I really envy you 
for climbing Kilimanjaro."

00:02:07.951 --> 00:02:11.451
He smiled at me and said, "Actually, 
I am going there again now."

00:02:11.451 --> 00:02:13.521
"No way! Please take me with you!"

00:02:14.341 --> 00:02:18.111
It turned out there was one place left
but I had to decide immediately.

00:02:18.441 --> 00:02:20.520
"OK, I am coming!" I said quickly.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.460
"But what will happen to your job?”
"Hmm... I’ll quit."

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.490
So before I realized it, I was on a plane,
traveling to Nairobi,

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.350
to arrive a few hours later in Tanzania,
to the safari capital, Arusha.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:39.040
So the next day, I could start to conquer
the snow-covered summit of Kilimanjaro.

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:40.449
Zsolt warned us,

00:02:40.449 --> 00:02:44.209
"Don't underestimate the mountain,
because Kilimanjaro is a tricky mountain,

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:47.307
where climbers actually
circumvent acclimatization,

00:02:47.307 --> 00:02:51.087
and instead of the ideal two weeks, 
they conquer the summit in a week.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:52.447
Which is dangerous.

00:02:52.687 --> 00:02:56.447
Because above 5, 000 meters, 
the level of oxygen is less than 50%,

00:02:56.447 --> 00:02:57.981
and if somebody isn't careful, 

00:02:57.981 --> 00:03:02.631
they can get a pulmonary embolism,
or cerebral edema, which could be fatal."

00:03:03.394 --> 00:03:05.594
Luckily I didn't have any problems,

00:03:05.594 --> 00:03:09.714
so I could concentrate all my energies 
on the natural wonders of Kilimanjaro.

00:03:10.604 --> 00:03:15.434
We reached the base camp 
at 4, 700 meters on the fifth day.

00:03:16.494 --> 00:03:18.534
However something happened there.

00:03:18.994 --> 00:03:23.474
We had dinner at five o'clock
and we discussed the summit attempt,

00:03:23.474 --> 00:03:28.994
but I felt so ill by then
that I could barely crawl to the tent.

00:03:29.064 --> 00:03:31.184
I entered, but collapsed from pain.

00:03:31.184 --> 00:03:33.684
Headache and nausea were crippling me.

00:03:33.702 --> 00:03:37.182
Although the entire expedition group
were there with a lot of advice,

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:39.502
none of it helped,
which made me feel worse.

00:03:39.502 --> 00:03:42.752
I felt that I was so close
to achieving my childhood dream,

00:03:42.752 --> 00:03:46.022
but I was simply not able
to take the final steps.

00:03:46.022 --> 00:03:48.162
I had never ever given up
on anything before,

00:03:48.162 --> 00:03:50.692
but the pain took me 
to the brink of giving up;

00:03:50.692 --> 00:03:53.282
I couldn't bear it.

00:03:54.298 --> 00:03:56.628
Then one of the guides came up to me.

00:03:56.628 --> 00:03:59.858
One whom I had I gotten to know
early on, and we had become friends.

00:03:59.858 --> 00:04:02.118
We shared some 
kind words every day,

00:04:02.118 --> 00:04:04.848
and he asked me, "What’s wrong Steve?"

00:04:05.308 --> 00:04:08.328
I explained it to him, and also,
that this was my dream!

00:04:08.328 --> 00:04:10.348
But I just saw it fading away.

00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:15.907
He was the only one who knew
the simple right answer;

00:04:15.907 --> 00:04:18.287
which was proper food and fluid intake.

00:04:18.287 --> 00:04:20.587
As it turned out, 
this had caused the problem.

00:04:21.012 --> 00:04:23.972
I trusted him and believed him.

00:04:23.972 --> 00:04:25.972
An hour and a half later
my pain was gone.

00:04:25.972 --> 00:04:28.972
I had no problem, so I was there,
just after one in the morning,

00:04:28.972 --> 00:04:33.262
with full gear, a huge smile on my face,
waiting for the start.

00:04:33.422 --> 00:04:35.780
Though I knew the hardest part
still lay ahead;

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.053
the steepest part of Kilimanjaro.

00:04:38.053 --> 00:04:41.973
All this at night, lit by headlamps,
in freezing wind and minus 17 degrees.

00:04:42.353 --> 00:04:44.282
But I was feeling strong.

00:04:44.282 --> 00:04:49.582
At the best moment, I reached 
Stella-point at a 5, 680 meter altitude,

00:04:49.582 --> 00:04:54.162
to see the African sunrise
from the most beautiful view.

00:04:54.723 --> 00:04:59.493
When clouds are 3, 500 meters below you,
and you look down on the sun,

00:04:59.493 --> 00:05:03.643
its colors and its view;
they are simply indescribable.

00:05:03.716 --> 00:05:07.716
And then I asked our mountain guide,
"Masu, how far is it to the summit?"

00:05:07.732 --> 00:05:10.302
And he told me, "About 250 meters."

00:05:10.302 --> 00:05:14.392
I was relieved by that because by then
I felt that I was running out of energy.

00:05:14.418 --> 00:05:18.798
He then added quietly,
"At least one and a half hours."

00:05:18.922 --> 00:05:22.012
"One and a half hours?" I said.
"At least? For just 250 meters?

00:05:22.012 --> 00:05:26.112
Are you kidding me?
I can run that in a minute!"

00:05:26.142 --> 00:05:29.092
Sure. But not here. Every single step
was a new challenge.

00:05:29.092 --> 00:05:32.555
Every single step is a new goal,
for which I had to fight for.

00:05:33.225 --> 00:05:36.345
But by the end, I was standing
on the highest point of Africa,

00:05:36.845 --> 00:05:39.918
on the 5, 895 meter-high point
of Kilimanjaro, the Uhuru-summit.

00:05:39.918 --> 00:05:43.038
I am not ashamed to admit
that I broke down in tears,

00:05:43.278 --> 00:05:47.278
because I made one
of my very first dreams come true.

00:05:49.176 --> 00:05:54.226
The story should end here actually,
here at this summit.

00:05:54.226 --> 00:05:57.006
But that wasn't the case.

00:05:58.077 --> 00:06:03.897
Because there he was; the young boy, 
to whom I had to be thankful for all this.

00:06:03.897 --> 00:06:06.838
In the next two days, we came down
from the mountain together.

00:06:06.838 --> 00:06:10.869
We laughed a lot, talked,
taught each other songs and words.

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:13.991
As we reached the foot of the mountain, 
I got to know Ombeni.

00:06:13.991 --> 00:06:17.211
His name was Ombeni, 
which means "praying man."

00:06:17.519 --> 00:06:20.919
I got to know his dreams,
and I knew what I was going to do.

00:06:21.571 --> 00:06:25.321
It was my turn now, I owed him one.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.601
But I realized, it was not that simple.

00:06:28.605 --> 00:06:31.247
It was much harder
than you would think.

00:06:31.247 --> 00:06:33.757
First, we organized 
an impromptu collection for him.

00:06:33.757 --> 00:06:35.757
but when he came
to our hotel, he said,

00:06:35.757 --> 00:06:38.440
"Steve would you bring
the package out to the street?

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.279
Because I will get caught 
and accused of stealing it."

00:06:42.573 --> 00:06:46.923
I did what he asked me of course.
In fact, I accompanied him home.

00:06:47.924 --> 00:06:51.474
And then I saw that Ombeni
was living in a slum,

00:06:52.604 --> 00:06:55.524
with mud-plastered walls
and rammed-earth flooring.

00:06:55.816 --> 00:06:58.826
We can call it "a woodshed."

00:07:00.547 --> 00:07:04.547
I wanted to take photos of inside, 
but I didn't want to offend him.

00:07:05.087 --> 00:07:07.717
Later on I overcame that fear
and I was right to do so.

00:07:07.717 --> 00:07:10.417
I learned that in Tanzania,
when they turn 18 years old,

00:07:10.417 --> 00:07:13.517
every young person is let out
of the family to live on their own.

00:07:13.517 --> 00:07:19.286
He was proud of saving 45 dollars
to get his own home.

00:07:19.293 --> 00:07:23.993
In fact, if he saved 65 dollars,
he could even have electricity in it.

00:07:24.832 --> 00:07:26.972
Because don't be fooled by the light!

00:07:27.158 --> 00:07:31.318
That is the light of my camera's flash,
not of the oil lamp you see there.

00:07:32.258 --> 00:07:34.858
I promised him
I would send hiking clothes,

00:07:34.858 --> 00:07:37.268
because I was double his size.

00:07:37.268 --> 00:07:38.668
So once I returned home,

00:07:38.668 --> 00:07:41.978
the next day, I went shopping
with my mother to get everything,

00:07:41.978 --> 00:07:44.628
and packed it into a large package.

00:07:45.568 --> 00:07:49.058
I realized then that I didn't have
anywhere to send it to.

00:07:49.548 --> 00:07:52.968
Slums don’t have street names
and house numbers.

00:07:54.208 --> 00:07:56.428
It was hard, but he got a PO box number,

00:07:56.428 --> 00:07:58.438
but then they told me at the post office,

00:07:58.438 --> 00:08:00.778
that packages can't be sent 
to PO box addresses.

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:05.961
Meanwhile days and weeks were passing by,
and I felt worse and worse,

00:08:05.998 --> 00:08:07.803
because I knew that he trusted me;

00:08:07.803 --> 00:08:11.463
I knew he believed that whatever I say,
it would just be that way.

00:08:11.463 --> 00:08:12.737
So when I got home,

00:08:12.737 --> 00:08:16.115
I sat back in my car and went back 
to the post office and said,

00:08:16.115 --> 00:08:18.375
"I'd like to send this package 
to that PO Box."

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:20.815
"You can't," they said.
"I don't care!" I said.

00:08:20.815 --> 00:08:23.745
"He might not get it!" they said.
"I don't care!" I said.

00:08:23.745 --> 00:08:26.644
"It will cost a lot," they said.
"I don't care!" I said.

00:08:26.914 --> 00:08:29.514
Finally, I managed to send it,
and he did get it,

00:08:29.514 --> 00:08:31.978
though he had to pay for it as well.

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:35.102
Meanwhile, I started looking
for a scholarship for him,

00:08:35.102 --> 00:08:39.982
because I knew that he had to stop
his hotel management studies.

00:08:40.042 --> 00:08:43.162
It was then when I realized
that while in the European Union

00:08:43.162 --> 00:08:46.622
it is not a problem to get
a scholarship for a young person,

00:08:46.752 --> 00:08:49.812
for a person from one 
of the poorest countries in the world -

00:08:49.812 --> 00:08:52.882
for someone who really needs it -
I really have no chance.

00:08:53.729 --> 00:08:56.639
Then I remembered a friend of mine,
who is a hotel-owner.

00:08:56.639 --> 00:08:58.649
I called him and I said,

00:08:58.649 --> 00:09:01.979
"Look, I’ll pay his airfare, 
he can stay at my place.

00:09:01.979 --> 00:09:04.919
Just let him work and study with you!"

00:09:06.202 --> 00:09:08.242
Then I remembered "The Little Prince."

00:09:08.962 --> 00:09:12.012
I remembered, what the Fox said to him:

00:09:12.536 --> 00:09:18.696
"You become responsible, forever,
for what you have tamed."

00:09:19.686 --> 00:09:21.036
How could I invite him here?

00:09:23.352 --> 00:09:29.522
To let him see how nice a restroom is here
compared to how his home looks?

00:09:29.762 --> 00:09:34.082
Everything kept pointing me 
in one direction: I had to give him money.

00:09:35.299 --> 00:09:36.679
But this was the hardest.

00:09:37.349 --> 00:09:39.489
I was not sure if I could trust him,

00:09:39.489 --> 00:09:42.439
that he would spend the money 
on what I gave it him for.

00:09:42.439 --> 00:09:45.689
I wrote a letter to him, asking him
to chat on Skype, and I told him:

00:09:45.689 --> 00:09:48.109
"Look, Ombeni; I promised
that I would help you.

00:09:48.109 --> 00:09:50.479
But I will only do this
if you spend this money

00:09:50.479 --> 00:09:52.359
on making your dream come true.

00:09:52.359 --> 00:09:53.309
And he promised.

00:09:55.479 --> 00:10:01.009
But I will admit, I was not 100% sure
that this would happen.

00:10:01.049 --> 00:10:02.929
But I didn't let him know.

00:10:02.929 --> 00:10:04.499
I wanted to trust him.

00:10:04.499 --> 00:10:08.469
I wanted him to see that I believed
that he could make his dream come true.

00:10:08.513 --> 00:10:12.694
But do not think that it is easier
to send money to a slum, than a package.

00:10:12.694 --> 00:10:15.534
After all, this was only happening
because of my expedition.

00:10:15.534 --> 00:10:19.414
Sometimes Ombeni sat on the street
for two days in front of our hotel

00:10:19.414 --> 00:10:21.024
so he didn't miss the alpinists.

00:10:21.164 --> 00:10:23.774
Meanwhile weeks and months passed

00:10:23.774 --> 00:10:30.414
and I got an email with a message in it,
about him getting his driver’s licence.

00:10:30.427 --> 00:10:33.797
Again, weeks and months later,
another email came with a message

00:10:33.797 --> 00:10:40.647
that he had returned to school
and finished his hotel management studies.

00:10:40.759 --> 00:10:44.639
After, not weeks, but months and years,

00:10:44.939 --> 00:10:48.039
he called me once on Skype
and sent me a file.

00:10:48.039 --> 00:10:50.619
In it, I found the certificate

00:10:51.099 --> 00:10:55.099
which proved that on 11th April 2014,
he made his childhood dream come true.

00:10:58.324 --> 00:11:01.884
The one he had told me about 
as we descended from the Kilimanjaro.

00:11:02.344 --> 00:11:05.934
He wanted his own mountain climbing
and safari agency.

00:11:05.934 --> 00:11:08.392
And he did it.

00:11:09.174 --> 00:11:14.024
It is called: Trust Tours
and Safaris Company.

00:11:15.061 --> 00:11:17.011
Thank you very much.

00:11:17.029 --> 00:11:19.969
(Applause)

